| Premise UX = UY gives a linear equation with coefficients {UX²: 1, UY²: -1}
| Then {AU²: 1, UY²: -1} + -1 x {UX²: 1, UY²: -1}
|    = {AU²: 1, UX²: -1}
We are left with a linear equation with coefficients {AU²: 1, UX²: -1} that gives UX = AU



058. | Angle Chasing to prove DZ ⟂ UZ:
| Premise ∠(AB,AO) = ∠(BO,AB) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AB: -2, AO: 1, BO: 1}
| Premise ∠(AC,AO) = ∠(CO,AC) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AC: -2, AO: 1, CO: 1}
| Then {AB: 1, AO: -1/2, BO: -1/2} + 1/2 x {AC: -2, AO: 1, CO: 1}
|    = {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2}
| Premise ∠(AD,AE) = ∠(DE,AD) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AD: -2, AE: 1, DE: 1}
| Then {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2} + -1/2 x {AD: -2, AE: 1, DE: 1}
|    = {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, AD: 1, AE: -1/2, DE: -1/2}
| Premise ∠(AD,DO) = ∠(AE,EO) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AD: -1, AE: 1, DO: 1, EO: -1}
| Then {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, AD: 1, AE: -1/2, DE: -1/2} + 1 x {AD: -1, AE: 1, DO: 1, EO: -1}
|    = {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, AE: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EO: -1}
| Premise ∠(AE,EO) = ∠(EO,EZ) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AE: -1, EO: 2, EZ: -1}
| Then {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, AE: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EO: -1} + 1/2 x {AE: -1, EO: 2, EZ: -1}
|    = {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EZ: -1/2}
| Premise ∠(AO,AZ) = ∠(AZ,OZ) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AO: 1, AZ: -2, OZ: 1}
| Then {AB: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EZ: -1/2} + 1 x {AO: 1, AZ: -2, OZ: 1}
|    = {AB: 1, AO: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EZ: -1/2, AZ: -2, OZ: 1}
| Premise ∠(AU,AX) = ∠(AX,UX) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AU: 1, AX: -2, UX: 1}
| Then {AB: 1, AO: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EZ: -1/2, AZ: -2, OZ: 1} + 1/2 x {AU: 1, AX: -2, UX: 1}
|    = {AB: 1, AO: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EZ: -1/2, AZ: -2, OZ: 1, AU: 1/2, AX: -1, UX: 1/2}
| Premise ∠(AU,AY) = ∠(AY,UY) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AU: 1, AY: -2, UY: 1}
| Then {AB: 1, AO: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EZ: -1/2, AZ: -2, OZ: 1, AU: 1/2, AX: -1, UX: 1/2} + 1/2 x {AU: 1, AY: -2, UY: 1}
|    = {AB: 1, AO: 1, BO: -1/2, AC: -1, CO: 1/2, DE: -1/2, DO: 1, EZ: -1/2, AZ: -2, OZ: 1, AU: 1, AX: -1, UX: 1/2, AY: -1, UY: 1/2}
| Premise ∠(AU,AZ) = ∠(AZ,UZ) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AU: 1, AZ: -2, UZ: 1}
